-- Rifts World Book 21: Splynn Dimensional Market - its bestiary and its notable NPCs.
-- 2 creatures (migration 074) and 0 notable NPCs (migration 072),
-- with their attacks in stat_attacks (migration 073).
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~369-splynn-animals.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/bestiary-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every
-- creature row passes creatureFormulaGaps, every value is printable ASCII,
-- and an 8-word shingle check of the prose fields against the book's cached text finds no copied run.

INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES
('demonrunner', 'Demonrunner', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Anarchist or miscreant', '{"IQ":"1D6","ME":"1D6+12","MA":"1D6+6","PS":"2D6+18","PP":"1D6+16","PE":"2D6+12","PB":"1D6+6","Spd":"1D6x10+120"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10+50+PE', '4D6', NULL, 'M.D.C. is 1D6x10+50 plus the P.E. attribute number. I.Q. is a high animal intelligence. P.S. and P.E. are supernatural. Speed: 130 (about 88 mph/141 km) is average and 180 (120 mph/192 km) the fastest; top speed lasts as many minutes as its P.E., then it slows to half or rests ten minutes. Half speed (about 40-50 mph) can be kept up for six hours, and a sprint 50% over top speed lasts 1D4 melee rounds, no more than once every two hours. Speed is 25% lower in forest or rough, rocky ground.', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":6,"strike":4,"parry":2,"roll":4}', 'Printed as R.C.C. bonuses, in addition to attribute bonuses: +6 initiative, +4 strike, +2 parry, +6 to automatic dodge (a dodge that costs no melee action), +4 roll with punch or impact, +3 to save vs Horror Factor, +1 to save vs poisons and toxins. Horror Factor 12 alone, 15 for a pack of four or more.', 'Printed as R.C.C. skills: a domesticated one can be trained to follow spoken commands about as well as an Earth dog. Natural prowl 60%, climb 25%, swim 45%.', 'Exceptional speed and stamina. Needs little water, drawing most of its fluid from the blood of its kills. Nightvision 1000 feet (305 m), sharp color vision, spots movement up to a mile (1.6 km) off, keen smell and hearing. Its semi-prehensile tail can strike. Leaps 100 feet (30.5 m) long and 50 feet (15.2 m) high after a short run, half that from a standstill, twice that at full speed. Prowl 60%, climb 25% (a flat-land runner), swim 45%.', 'None.', 'None.', '8-10 feet (2.4-3 m) long plus a 2-4 foot (0.6-1.2 m) tail; 3.5-4 feet (1.1-1.2 m) at the shoulder, head carried low', '400-800 lbs (180-360 kg)', '30-40 years; up to 60 in captivity away from violence', 'Open plains, prairie, savannah and grassland; copes with light forest and city streets or ruins, but shuns dense forest and mountains. Escaped animals roam the American West, the African savannah and the plains of Atlantis.', 'None as such; it runs in packs of its own kind, keeps to itself when alone, and may carry Simvan Monster Riders and other lovers of speed.', 'Bigger, stronger predators; nobody else in particular.', 'None. The book labels its bonuses and skills R.C.C., but heads it a slave animal and does not offer it to players.', 'A long, four-legged predator from open plains, built like a cat crossed with a dinosaur and given a demon''s face, with claws that half retract at a run and a flattened tail it steers with. Among the fastest runners anywhere, it outpaces a hovercycle. A pack animal that follows its strongest member, it obeys a firm master and turns on a weak or hesitant one. The Splugorth slavers sell it as a mount, hunting beast, guard and pet, and Splynn races it and sets packs of 2-4 on a dozen unarmed Juicers and cyborgs in the Demonrunner Murderthon. Riders take -20% on riding skill even when expert with exotic animals. Value: 100,000 credits untamed, 250,000 credits trained for hunting or riding; prices double or triple after a Murderthon.', 'Rifts World Book 21: Splynn Dimensional Market p.71-73'),
('kryygorth-shellback', 'Kryygorth Shellback', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Unprincipled or anarchist; a herbivore', '{"IQ":"1D4+1","ME":"1D6+2","MA":"1D6","PS":"1D6+28","PP":"1D6+4","PE":"1D6+32","PB":"2D4","Spd":"1D6+12"}', NULL, NULL, '3D6x10+200', '3D6', NULL, 'M.D.C. by location; the mdc formula is the outer shell (main body). Head 80+1D4x10; eyes (4, one pair hidden under the head plating) 6 each, hit only at -8 even with a Called Strike, and losing them leaves it blind and nearly helpless; legs (6) 90+2D6 each; outer shell main body 3D6x10+200; soft underbody 1D6x10+100. Destroying the head, the shell or the underbody kills it. I.Q. is a low animal intelligence; P.S. and endurance are supernatural.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":3,"strike":1,"parry":1}', '+1 strike and parry, +6 to save vs poison and disease, +4 to save vs Horror Factor, plus attribute bonuses. Horror Factor 10 only to those who do not know what it is, none to those who know it is nearly harmless. It fights only until a threat is driven off.', NULL, 'Natural M.D.C. armor, enormous endurance and strength (one can pull well over ten tons, and it seems never to tire), swim 65%, senses water within one mile (1.6 km). Takes half damage from fire, cold and disease.', 'None.', 'None.', 'About 10 feet (3 m) long, 6 feet (1.8 m) tall and 5 feet (1.5 m) wide', '2-4 tons', 'One to five years when raised for slaughter; up to 35 years possible', 'Grassy plains and light forest, always within Splugorth territory and seldom off the farms. On Rifts Earth: the farmlands of Atlantis, the Phoenix Empire in Africa and the Splugorth colonies at Newfoundland, with a few perhaps elsewhere.', NULL, 'The Kryygorth Hunter preys on it; otherwise none, unless the Minions of Splugorth who eat it count.', 'None; an NPC animal.', 'A heavy, armored grazer like a huge beetle speckled blue and green, with a long rounded head and a pair of horns it uses to strip bark, dig roots and defend itself. One of the creations of Lord Kryygorth that outlived him, it is now herded across the Splugorth holdings as their favorite livestock: its meat feeds the Splugorth and their Minions (and humans like it too), its shell becomes M.D.C. armor, and the Gargoyle and Brodkil Empires buy the butchered meat, as do Splynn''s shops and restaurants. Placid and stupid as cattle, it is a tireless draft or riding beast for anyone in no hurry, and a water-finder; only rarely is a live one offered to outsiders. Value: about 20,000 credits for a riding animal; a breeding male or female is rare and costs over a million; its meat goes for 5-10 credits per pound (0.45 kg) by cut.', 'Rifts World Book 21: Splynn Dimensional Market p.79-80');

